properties.rationale:
Fixes the cause found in fact:search-design-did-not-find-a-change-event-by-the-error-its-rationale-quotes-2026-10-12. Searchability was a hand-set flag per property, and nothing checked that prose fields were covered.

Built on Anthony's "I'd like to take on all these in this session" (2026-10-12), from the fix the root cause proposed:
1. the flags;
2. a failing-first test;
3. the description says what search reads.

Two things it added:
- A WIDER CLASS. The test sorts every one of the 96 unsearched string properties. It found 9 prose fields beyond the root cause's 6, and gives the other 81 a reason each.
- THE RE-INDEX. Servers already rebuilt the index at every start, through new_reporting. The one-shot --call door's open compared only document counts, which a new flag on an indexed type leaves unchanged. So the index now records a hash of the properties it was built over (Schema::fulltext_stamp). It is kept as a plain file beside Tantivy's own, because Tantivy's garbage collection deletes the managed files a commit stops referencing. Any rebuild writes it after its commit. An index created empty under this build writes it at creation, so a new design never reports a rebuild.

Known limit: if an older build writes to a store after this one has recorded the hash, the hash is not moved, so those nodes' new fields stay unsearched until a rebuild. reindex_search, or any server start, rebuilds.

Checks:
- failing-first, then cargo test --workspace (385 test binaries);
- clippy for both configurations, and cargo fmt;
- toolsnap: search_design only;
- the Python CI gates.

